# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Editors / OS ───────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log

# ── Claude Code local config (local-only, no secrets) ──
.claude/

# ── Local-only docs (meeting prep, not for the shared repo) ──
docs/CUE_CARD.md

# ── Large / regenerable data — keep OUT of git ─────────
# NOTE: comments must be on their own line; git ignores inline (trailing) comments.
# PDFs/                -> 2.1 GB corpus (re-downloadable via setup/)
# *.pdf                -> copyrighted source papers — never redistribute
# chroma_db/           -> 464 MB vector index (rebuild: core/rag_pipeline.py --rebuild)
# chroma_db_clean/     -> 268 MB clean index (owf_clean_v1); rebuild via core/clean_index/.
#                         chroma.sqlite3 alone is 212 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
# chunks_metadata.json -> 10.9 MB, regenerated on every index rebuild
# archive/frozen_study.zip
#                      -> 245 MB zip of the withdrawn pilot, also past the 100 MB limit.
#                         Its four artefacts are tracked unzipped in archive/frozen_study/.
PDFs/
*.pdf
chroma_db/
chroma_db_clean/
chunks_metadata.json
archive/frozen_study.zip

# Tracked on purpose (small scientific record): pilot_eval_set.json,
# contradictions_cache.json, results_cache.jsonl, results.csv,
# retrieval_evaluation.json, paper_metadata.json, and the DOI/query provenance .txt files.
